    "buildCommand": null,
    "testCommand": "cd /Users/jaesolshin/Documents/GitHub/odl-vl\ngit reset --soft e98960e >/dev/null 2>&1\ngit restore --staged . 2>/dev/null\ngit add src/odl_vl/pipeline/output.py tests/test_pipeline_figcaption.py\ngit commit -F - -- src/odl_vl/pipeline/output.py tests/test_pipeline_figcaption.py <<'MSG'\nfix(figures): consistent caption-title bold and drop equation strips mis-detected as figures\n\nFound while generalizing to other papers (arXiv preprint, thesis):\n\n- Caption bold: the label+title bold normalization only matched a period\n  separator with a terminal-period title, so colon-labelled captions\n  ('Figure 3: Title.') and period-less titles ('Table 1. Range of methods')\n  fell through and kept the VLM's inconsistent bold. Widen the pattern to accept\n  '.', ':' or no separator, and a title ending at the first period OR line end.\n\n- Equation images: ODL flags some display equations as raster figures, so the\n  same math rendered inconsistently -- some as LaTeX, some as a cropped image.\n  Drop a thin horizontal figure strip (h < 40 and w > 3h) ONLY when its page\n  actually contains display math, so height is never the sole basis for removing\n  a figure: a thin real graphic on a non-math page is kept (e.g. CSNL's 'Check\n  for updates' logo, which the height-only rule wrongly dropped). The VLM's LaTeX\n  carries the equation, so nothing is lost (RATS drops 14 equation strips on\n  math pages and keeps 5 figures; CSNL and Latimer drop 0).\n\nTests: figcaption caption-format + equation-strip shape + page-math gate.\nMSG\necho \"=== result: one figures commit, no dup ===\"\ngit --no-pager log --oneline -4\necho \"--- files ---\"\ngit --no-pager show --stat --oneline HEAD | head -5\necho \"=== final full suite ===\"\n( cd tests && uv run --no-sync python -m pytest -q 2>&1 | tail -2 )",
